IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssaa-claimant`
IMPORT `ssaa-instruments`

-- Social Security (Administration) Act instruments -- worked cases, from the claimant's and jobseeker's seat (REQ-0106).
-- Expected values were written by hand from the deposited determinations (F2018L00971, F2026L01408, F2018L00779,
-- F2022C00591), never copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.

-- s 14A. She phones on 1 March 2027 after leaving a violent partner, and lodges on 10 March: her claim dates from 1 March.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim taken to be made, with the s 14A class` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 3 2027) `domestic or family violence` TRUE TRUE FALSE `none of these` EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- No listed circumstance: the claim is made on the day lodged.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim taken to be made, with the s 14A class` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 3 2027) `none of these` TRUE TRUE FALSE `none of these` EQUALS Date 10 3 2027
-- A listed circumstance that did not stop her lodging on the day of contact: not in the class.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim taken to be made, with the s 14A class` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 3 2027) `living in, and being in, a remote area` FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of these` EQUALS Date 10 3 2027
-- In hospital, lodging 61 days after contact with the Secretary satisfied her medical condition delayed her: 1 March.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim taken to be made, with the s 14A class` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 5 2027) `hospital, or a temporary incapacity from a medical condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE `I had a medical condition that significantly hindered me` EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `I am in the s 14A class` `a child of mine born in those 8 weeks` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `I am in the s 14A class` `none of these` TRUE

-- s 42AC(3). Required 20 job searches, made 15: not adequate; made 20: adequate on the number, quality may be assessed.
#ASSERT `Were my job search efforts adequate` 15 20 EQUALS `not adequate: I did not make the number of job searches I was required to make (Job Search Efforts Determination s 6(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Were my job search efforts adequate` 20 20 EQUALS `adequate on the number; the Secretary may still look at their quality (good faith, a variety of jobs, fields and methods) or other matters before deciding (s 6(1)(b), (2))`
#ASSERT `Is my job search shortfall a mutual obligation failure` TRUE 15 20
#ASSERT NOT `Is my job search shortfall a mutual obligation failure` TRUE 20 20
#ASSERT NOT `Is my job search shortfall a mutual obligation failure` FALSE 15 20

-- s 42AI. Missed an appointment because she was at a job interview, which the Secretary accepts directly prevented her.
#ASSERT `Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` `I was at a job interview at the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is a matter the Secretary must take into account in deciding whether I had a reasonable excuse (Reasonable Excuse Determination s 5)`
-- Unforeseen caring duties, but the Secretary is not satisfied they directly prevented her.
#ASSERT `Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` `unforeseen family or caring responsibilities` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it must not be taken into account: the Secretary is not satisfied it directly prevented me from meeting the requirement (s 6(3))`
-- Alcohol dependency, after an earlier excused failure and a refused referral to treatment.
#ASSERT `Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` `a drug or alcohol dependency` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it must not be taken into account: an earlier failure was excused for drug or alcohol dependency and I refused or failed to take part in the treatment I was referred to (s 6(4))`
-- ... unless the treatment was not available to him.
#ASSERT `Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` `a drug or alcohol dependency` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it is a matter the Secretary must take into account in deciding whether I had a reasonable excuse (Reasonable Excuse Determination s 5)`
#ASSERT `Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` `another reason` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is not one of the listed matters; the Secretary may still consider it, since the list is of matters that must be taken into account`

-- s 42AR, Non-Compliance Determination s 5. Inputs: demerits in 6 active months; one of the serious kinds; DHS assessment
-- complete; this failure within 3 active months of it; already found persistent in the last 3 active months; any demerit
-- failure in the last 3 active months.
#ASSERT `Are my failures persistent` 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Three demerits, one for skipping a job interview: the threshold is met with fewer.
#ASSERT `Are my failures persistent` 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Are my failures persistent` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Five demerits but the assessment has not happened.
#ASSERT NOT `Are my failures persistent` 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- No failure with a demerit in the 3 active months before this one: never persistent (s 5(5)).
#ASSERT NOT `Are my failures persistent` 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Already found persistent within the last 3 active months (s 5(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Are my failures persistent` 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- Non-Compliance Determination s 6.
#ASSERT `How much can my instalment be cut` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `half of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(a); Non-Compliance Determination s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `How much can my instalment be cut` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the whole of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(b); s 6(2))`
#ASSERT `How much can my instalment be cut` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `half of one instalment: the first failure after my payment was cancelled (s 6(4))`
